      {
        "id": 205920,
        "name": "Demiher0",
        "username": "Demiher0",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/demiher0/{size}/1931_2.png",
        "created_at": "2018-02-26T11:46:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The most recent RPG&nbsp;I played time wise is DnD 5th ed. I am in the middle of getting my players ready for a Dresden Files RPG game that should scratch my DM itch to replace the aborted game of Spellbound Kingdoms I had to end due to having to move.</p><p>I run a monthly one shot of a system that is not DnD/Pathfinder/Fate for my FLGS because I like showing people the breadth of the hobby&nbsp;<span>(Totaly hasn't been the starter kit the past few months)&nbsp;</span></p><p><span>Systems I have run over time are many and varied. Mutants and Masterminds, Mage the Awakening, Shadowrun 20th Aniversary are the games that really stuck with me as a DM. I have also used a fair few PBTA games such as Apocalypse&nbsp;World, Dungeon World, Masks, Urban Shadows, and a few nicher games using the PBTA system like Bronze Circle, Enemy Action, and Fury. Yet I still want to play and run more systems there are so many and so little time for gaming.</span></p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:35:19.286Z",
